WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.211
Database design comes before trustworthy analysis If

00:00:05.224 --> 00:00:07.829
the structure is unclear even a syntactically

00:00:07.856 --> 00:00:10.750
correct query can produce confusing or unreliable

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.569
results That is why we begin by

00:00:13.595 --> 00:00:15.424
deciding what we are modeling and what

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.148
one row in each table should mean

00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:21.661
A practical design process starts with scope

00:00:22.584 --> 00:00:26.176
What real-world problem are we representing Then

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:28.400
we identify the main entities connect them

00:00:28.426 --> 00:00:30.847
through relationships and define rules that must

00:00:30.874 --> 00:00:35.946
always hold Normalization helps us reduce
unnecessary

00:00:35.972 --> 00:00:39.143
repetition while constraints help prevent invalid
data

00:00:39.157 --> 00:00:43.212
from entering the database A useful final

00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:45.633
question is this if a different application

00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:48.343
inserts data tomorrow will the database itself

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.820
still protect the important rules Good design

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:53.833
should not depend only on one user

00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:55.109
remembering what to do
